      "type": "paragraph",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "so well known to devour children and adults.—Vikrama[*]'s",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "Ruins have been further out than",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "all pointed at",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "as a temple and called \"Bhartṛihari's",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "Cave\" is reached by an",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "in which he",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "is said to make his offerings and it is supposed that the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "eastern passage to Benares which",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "was",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "way is now blocked up by a massive block of stone",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "the entrance in the of the cave",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "was and its side has two windows and",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 13,
          "text": "are interpreted to be the marks left by Bhartṛihari's hands",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 14,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 15,
          "text": "used to support the roof from falling.[†]",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": true,
      "note": "Page is severely damaged and illegible in large parts; much of r1 and r2 is reconstructed or partial."
    },
    {
      "id": "r2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "But leaving aside for the present such traditions, some of the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "principal ones of which will have to be noticed in a",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "suitable place in the sequel, let us first turn to a question",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "which lies on the very threshold of our inquiry. What is",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "this work, and who is the real author of it? Writing in",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "1801, speaking of Bhartṛihari, Colebrooke said: \"Whether any",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "beautiful poems have been composed by him, besides the mor-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "al reflections which the poet is supposed to make on the dis-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "covery of his wife's infidelity. It consists of either three or four",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "S'atakas or centuries of couplets.\"[‡] In this passage,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "we cannot but think that the learned writer has been betrayed",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "into some inaccuracy. In the first place, it is only the sec-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 13,
          "text": "ond stanza of the Nîtis'ataka which lends any support to the",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": true,
      "note": "Heavily degraded scan; first two lines of the paragraph are above line 1 marker in the cutout."
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "footnote",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "* Vol. VI. and Colebrooke's Essays (Madras Reprint 1872)",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "Vol. II. p. 175. Dr. Kern, in his Preface to the Bṛihatsaṁhitâ,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "discussing the popular notion of Vikrama's being the founder of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "the Samvat Era, says that the \"objections that may be raised",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": true,
      "note": "Very faint and blotchy; line 4 actually has two lines of text in the cutout ('to the opinion are many and formidable.\"—Vide infra')."
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "footnote",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "† I state this from a verbal communication from a friend who was in those parts for some time.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": true,
      "note": "Two printed lines grouped under line marker 1; very faint."
    },
    {
